2. Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. **Join the call** on the townhall page, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.
3. When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows "Missed N townhalls" for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.
4. The deck''s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role''s numbers for the week. Press **Add a shout-out** on a tile to add yours.

## Where staff live (release 35)

Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.</p><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-portals-and-sign-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Portals and sign-in</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Portals and view as</b>. Every portal has a card.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each card links to <b class="gd-ui">Its sign-in page</b>, the address to send that person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a person in the list on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open as this person</b> to see that portal as they see it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The site&#39;s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend&#39;s test inboxes) are marked &quot;Test account&quot; in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:65.9%;top:30.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:58.1%;top:39.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.6%;top:45.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-invite-a-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Invite a person</h2><p class="gd-p">Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Name and Email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>. The link in the email works for 24 hours.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/360"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="360"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:66.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.8%;top:87.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People &gt; Owners and People &gt; Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-add-an-investor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add an investor</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add an investor</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer&#39;s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Invite now is ticked: press <b class="gd-ui">Add and invite</b>. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-send-a-password-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send a password link</h2><p class="gd-p">For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On their row, press <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>. They get &quot;Reset your CarmaCars password&quot;, valid for 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> on the same row opens their portal, read only.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/440"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="440"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.8%;top:6.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.2%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.1%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-view-as-see-what-someone-sees" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">View as: see what someone sees</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A red banner says &quot;Viewing as Name (email), read only.&quot; on every page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Exit</b> to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/620"><img src="/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="620"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Can&#39;t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-audit-log" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The audit log</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Logs</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Changes</b> tab, shows who changed what, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Search by table, record id or value.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/audit</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.6%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:39%;top:46.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.6%;top:20.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-and-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff and roles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> opens Staff and roles.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row has <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">End access</b> to close their staff portal at once. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> undoes it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/780"><img src="/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="780"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:59%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:86.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:92.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-admin-access" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Admin access</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site&#39;s nightly checks sign in with.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change the list only if the business&#39;s Admin address changes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-scorecards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff scorecards</h2><p class="gd-p">See how each assistant is doing against the targets.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/350"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="350"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.1%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales by staff member</h2><p class="gd-p">See each person&#39;s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> or <b class="gd-ui">By month</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Commission rate</b> gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. <b class="gd-ui">Home address</b> here changes it if it is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The whole team: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to</td><td>Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-staff-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales staff: in person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Work mode</b> on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month&#39;s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a remote person&#39;s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rates</td><td>In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Remote minimum</td><td>400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings &gt; Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-an-admin-has-every-staff-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An Admin has every staff page</h2><p class="gd-p">An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-two-records-of-one-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Two records of one person</h2><p class="gd-p">When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: &quot;Your CarmaCars accounts are now one&quot;. A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> under the renter still works as before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Two different people after all? Press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-new-staff-the-academy-then-the-agreement-then-the-portal" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: the academy first, then their staff agreement, then everything else. Until the academy is passed they open only the academy, the guide, their profile and <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>; after it, until the agreement is signed, only Welcome, their profile and their documents to sign.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire&#39;s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Staff agreements</b>: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire&#39;s licence number), and <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the academy and the agreement are done, shows the team&#39;s WhatsApp group (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp team group link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp Sales group link</b>; empty until you set them). The same link goes by email, once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-accounts-locked-for-inactivity" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Accounts locked for inactivity</h2><p class="gd-p">A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Staff inactive lock days</b>) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees &quot;Account locked for inactivity&quot; when they sign in. You get an alert. On <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> the row says <b class="gd-ui">Locked for inactivity</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b>. The staff list shows each person&#39;s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-hours-and-the-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hours and the townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Breaks and idle time (release 35).</b> Customer service, Fleet and Finance press <b class="gd-ui">Start break</b> and <b class="gd-ui">End break</b> next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>, each person&#39;s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period&#39;s breaks).</p><p class="gd-p">While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, &quot;Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min&quot;, and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with <b class="gd-ui">Set Quo user</b> on Timesheet; the <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Idle minutes</b> against kpi_idle_minutes_week.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 1:00 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week&#39;s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; <b class="gd-ui">Build again</b> refreshes the numbers. Set the call link in Program settings; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-townhall-day-attendance-and-the-team-slide-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time. To change it, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the day or time</b> on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website&#39;s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants&#39; live calls always take the hour before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on the townhall page, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows &quot;Missed N townhalls&quot; for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The deck&#39;s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role&#39;s numbers for the week. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a shout-out</b> on a tile to add yours.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-where-staff-live-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where staff live (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'your-workday', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.

## The menu

Every office role has the same short menu: **To do** (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one **More** for the rest of your work, **Bookings** (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and **Me** (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: **Send an offer** and **New quote** on Requests, **Add a rental** on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters'' phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.

A **More** page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.

| Function | Your links, then More |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur |
| Sales | Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur |
| Fleet | Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button) |
| Finance | Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance bills |

## To do

Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.

1. The top shows your function, today''s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.
2. **Next up** is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or **Take it** to make it yours.
3. Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.
4. Customer service and Sales: **Waiting for a reply** lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today''s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.
5. **Every open task**: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.
6. Press **Take it** to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. **Sheet** opens the step-by-step procedure.
7. Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day''s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.
8. On a computer, press **/** to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 48.6 20.2, 2 31.9 52.1, 3 41.7 72.3")

## Work a task

Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.

| Button | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Open the working screen** | Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about. |
| **Done** | You finished it. It leaves the queue. |
| **Waiting** | You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours. |
| **Escalate** | It needs an Admin. Add why. |
| **Hand over** | Give it to someone else on the team. |
| **Add a note** | Leave a note for whoever looks next. |

> Tip: Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.

## Today

1. Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.
2. Press a booking number to open it. **To do** takes you back to your tasks.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 700; address: carmacars.ca/va/today; pins: 1 22.9 24.6")

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. The queue shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, hours, rate and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Several functions? Switch with Working as

If you cover more than one function, **Working as** above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.

## Your scorecard

1. Open **Me** (the **Scorecard** tab).
2. By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.
4. The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 360; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 1 4.2 39.7, 2 62.5 58.3")

## Clock in and out

Customer service, Fleet and Finance: press **Clock in** on your home page when you start and **Clock out** when you stop. **My hours** shows today, the week and every entry. You are reminded if you have not clocked in 15 minutes after your start time.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: the academy first, then your staff agreement (it opens for signing once the academy is passed), then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show the team''s WhatsApp group: join it, then press **I joined**.

## The weekly townhall

**Me** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call''s deck, the next call time and its link. **Add to my calendar** adds the call every week.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)

**KPIs by week** sits on **My scorecard**: your role''s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.

## Your schedule, hours and pay

**Hours** > **Schedule** shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.

| Role | Schedule |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | 6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off |
| Finance | Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work |
| Fleet | 6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off |

1. Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.
2. You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under **Hours** > **My hours**, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.
3. Finance prepares the payroll under **Hours** > **Payroll**: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then **Send for approval**. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.

## The townhall''s 30 minutes

The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press **Join now** (from 15 minutes before), then **Confirm I am in the call** on the Townhall page, or press **Check in**: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? **Tell yours** under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week''s recording is listed on the Townhall page.

> Watch out: Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it.', 'Your workday', 'The menu, To do, task actions, Today, switching functions and your scorecard.',
